                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chris Cain",
                        "email": "cjcain@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "cjcain"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks good, but I would like the commit message tweaked a bit to emphasize the changes. Something like:\n\nRemove support for P8 and P9 processors\n\nStarting with this commit, occ-control will no longer support the following:\n- P8 Processors (uses I2C communication with the OCCs)\n- P9 Processors (uses SBEFIFO for communication with the OCCs)\n\nThis commit has no changes to occ-control functionality for P10 and newer processors.\nThis change cleans up the code and removes redundant compiler flags."
                }
            ],
